			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Description" "DNP by default. Optional feedforward capacitor across R8 (VOUT to FB). TI SLUSEG9E Sec 8.2.2.3: 'A feedforward capacitor reduces the output ripple in PSM and improves the load transient response. A 120pF capacitor is good for the 1.8V output typical application.' That value is for 1.8 V (smaller R1); at 3.3 V with R1 = 453k the zero lands at 1/(2*pi*453k*120p) = 2.9 kHz, so 120 pF is a starting point, not a verified value. Table 8-3 note 4: needs Cout >= 22uF (C21 = 22uF OK). FIXED 2026-11-17: previously wired VOUT-to-GND, contradicting this description. Fit and tune only after measuring PSM ripple on TP403/TP401."
			(at 138.43 93.98 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
